  <event id="344">
      <start>15:00</start>
      <duration>00:25</duration>
      <room>H.1309</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Replication features of 2011: what they were, how to get and how to use them</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>MySQL and Friends Devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The year 2011 saw a lot of work being done on replication in MySQL world. Different implementations of the same feature were produced, compared, and put into releases.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk present an easy-to-understand summary of the results: - What exactly are the new features - Where they have/will be released - What are the differences between implementations in various MySQL branches&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We will also discuss how the new improvements relate to alternative replication solutions like Galera or Tungsten.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description></description>
      <persons>
          <person id="3441">Sergey Petrunya</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>